==Galician==

===Etymology===
From Old Galician and {{inh|pt|roa-opt|prouar}}, from {{inh|gl|la|probō|probāre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|/pɾoˈβaɾ/}}

===Verb===
{{gl-verb|prob|ar}}

# to [[prove]] {{gloss|to demonstrate that something is true or viable; to give proof for}}
#: {{syn|gl|demostrar}}
# to [[prove]] {{gloss|to put to the test, to make trial of}}
#* '''c1295''', R. Lorenzo (ed.), ''La traducción gallega de la Crónica General y de la Crónica de Castilla''. Ourense: I.E.O.P.F., page 806:
#*: '''prouarõ''' tres escaleyras de fuste et acharõnas curtas; et desi atarõnas a hũa cõ a outra et deytarõnas a hũa torre''
#*:: they '''tried''' three wooden ladders but found them too short; and so they tied them together and leaned them against a tower 
#: {{uxi|gl|q=proverb|Ata que probes non aprobes.|Untill you prove, don't approve.}}
#: {{uxi|gl|q=proverb|Antes que probedes, non gabedes.|Before you prove, don't praise.}}
#: {{syn|gl|comprobar}}
# to [[try]]

====Conjugation====
{{gl-conj-ar|prob}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|gl|aprobar}}
* {{l|gl|proba}}

