==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|la|probāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|probō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{es-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb|prob|ar|pres=pruebo}}

# to [[prove]]
#: {{uxi|es|No puedes '''probar'''lo.|You can’t '''prove''' it.}}
# to [[test]], to [[demonstrate]]
# to [[taste]]
#: {{uxi|es|'''Prueba''' a ver si está bueno.|'''Taste''' it to see if it’s good.}}
# to [[try]], to [[try out]], to [[sample]], to [[test]] [[out]], to [[give]] a [[go]], to [[have a go]]
#: {{uxi|es|Lo '''probó''' todo sin éxito.|He '''tried''' everything without success.}}
# to [[check out]], to [[probe]]
# to [[suit]]
#: {{uxi|es|Vivir en Madrid no le '''prueba'''.|Living in Madrid doesn't '''suit''' her.}}
# to [[try out]] {{gloss|for a team}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive|with clothes, etc.}} to [[try on]], see if it [[fit]]s
#: {{uxi|es|María '''se probó''' el vestido.|Maria '''tried on''' the dress.}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive}} to [[prove oneself]], to prove to oneself
# {{lb|es|reflexive}} to be [[tested]], to be [[proved]], to be [[proven]]

